<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.game-center</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- iCloud (finding #4, COMPLIANCE_CHECKLIST.md): CloudSaveStore.swift calls
	     FileManager.url(forUbiquityContainerIdentifier: nil), which needs an
	     icloud-container-identifiers + icloud-services entry here to ever
	     resolve non-nil — right now it silently always returns nil, so cloud
	     sync never activates. NOT added yet: confirmed by an actual device
	     build attempt (2026-09-05) that Apple's free/personal developer team
	     ("Oguzcan Budak") cannot provision the iCloud capability at all —
	     "Personal development teams... do not support the iCloud capability."
	     This requires enrolling in the paid Apple Developer Program
	     ($99/year) — an account-level action only the user can take. Once
	     enrolled, add:
	       <key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
	       <array><string>iCloud.com.dreamhaven.dreamkeepers</string></array>
	       <key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
	       <array><string>CloudDocuments</string></array>
	       <key>com.apple.developer.ubiquity-kvstore-identifier</key>
	       <string>$(TeamIdentifierPrefix)com.dreamhaven.dreamkeepers</string>
	     and create the matching iCloud container in the Apple Developer
	     portal (or let Xcode's "Signing & Capabilities" tab do both at once
	     by ticking iCloud → CloudKit/Documents there instead of editing this
	     file by hand). -->
</dict>
</plist>
